# Package ids published to nuget.org, one per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
# The release workflow names each id explicitly in its push and its GitHub release, and
# PackagesPushTests holds this file to both of those and to what the solution packs. Adding a
# packable project without classifying it FAILS THE SUITE, which is the whole point: the alternative
# is discovering it after a permanent publish. scripts/repo-conventions.cs reads it too: an id here
# is what makes `nuget` a topic this repository must carry.
#
# ⛔ Every id here must be covered by the repository's ONE trusted-publishing policy. nuget.org
# mints one API key per token exchange scoped to one matching policy, so a policy per id does not
# work: the first id publishes permanently and the rest are rejected 403 in the same command.

Bennewitz.Ninja.DiffView.Core
Bennewitz.Ninja.DiffView.Avalonia
